# KEYS: nsxiv

## Navigation & Panning

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| **h / j / k / l** | Pan image Left / Down / Up / Right |
| **n / p** | Move to the Next / Previous image in directory |
| **Enter** | Toggle between Single Image and Thumbnail mode |
| **f** | Toggle Fullscreen mode |
| **g** | Go to the first image |
| **G** | Go to the last image |

---

## Zooming & Scaling

| Key | Action |
| :--- | :--- |
| **+** / **=** | Zoom In |
| **-** | Zoom Out |
| **w** | Zoom to fit the window |
| **e** | Zoom to fit the image width to window |
| **H** | Zoom to fit the image height to window |
| **1** | Zoom to 100% (Actual size) |

---

## Image Operations

* **r** - Reload the image (useful if the file has changed on disk).
* **m** - Mark/unmark the current image (marks are passed to stdout on exit).
* **ctrl-x** - Run an external command (requires script at `~/.config/nsxiv/exec/key-handler`).
* **[** / **]** - Rotate image 90° counter-clockwise / clockwise.
* **\** - Flip image horizontally.

---

## Thumbnail Mode Commands

* **j / k / h / l** - Navigate the grid.
* **Enter** - Open the selected image.
* **m** - Mark/unmark the highlighted image.
* **q** - Close thumbnail mode (back to single image or exit).

